title: "HIV Drug Resistance Prediction with ESM-2 Protein Language Model"
version: 1.0.2
date-released: 2026-06-08
url: "https://github.com/hayden-farquhar/HIV-ESM-2"
repository-code: "https://github.com/hayden-farquhar/HIV-ESM-2"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - HIV drug resistance
  - protein language models
  - ESM-2
  - antiretroviral therapy
  - machine learning
  - drug resistance mutations
abstract: >-
  A machine learning pipeline for predicting HIV drug resistance from
  protein sequences using ESM-2 protein language model embeddings. Under
  nested cross-validation across 18 antiretroviral drugs, ESM-2 embeddings
  achieve performance comparable to traditional sparse mutation encodings
  (0.9404-0.9487 mean AUC vs 0.9466 baseline) without requiring explicit
  mutation calling against reference sequences. High-attribution positions
  show enrichment for known drug resistance mutations (averaging 3.2x to 6.1x
  across top-ranked residues, with statistically significant enrichment in
  approximately 35% of per-drug tests), with lower significance in protease inhibitors.
